step Leatherworking recipes at 213
  tip Nightscape Pants (from 205) is taught only by the Artisan trainers: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). You can train Artisan there now if you are level 35 (it needs Leatherworking 200), which saves the trip at 225.
  learn 10548 npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  learn 10548 npc 11098 only Horde
  train Leatherworking Artisan optional

step Nightscape Pants to 225
  tip Nightscape Pants is orange at 213 (yellow 225, green 235, grey 245): about 12 crafts to 225, a point every craft. Each takes 14 Thick Leather and 4 Silken Thread. The trainer teaches it, and it is the cheapest way through these points in the data. Leatherworking 225 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 10548 until 225
  skill Leatherworking 225

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan (225-300)
section Leatherworking 225-300

step Artisan Leatherworking
  tip Artisan raises the cap from 225 to 300; it needs Leatherworking 200 and character level 35, so you can take it on any visit from 200. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands); Horde Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas). This route trains it at Drakk Stonehand (The Hinterlands) for the Alliance and Hahrana Ironhide (Feralas) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 225-300: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Rugged Armor Kit (from 225). 225-300 takes about 3g 40s of recipes and 44g 90s of vendor goods, plus 1205 Rugged Leather and 500 Runecloth to gather or buy.
  level 35
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  train Leatherworking Artisan npc 11098 only Horde
  learn 19058 npc 11097 only Alliance map 1425
  learn 19058 npc 11098 only Horde

step Leatherworking 225-300: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 39 Black Dye (3g 90s) and 82 Rune Thread (41g); about 44g 90s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya and Tamar).
  buy 2325 x39 nearest
  buy 14341 x82 nearest

step Pattern: Wicked Leather Gauntlets
  tip Pattern: Wicked Leather Gauntlets teaches Wicked Leather Gauntlets (Leatherworking 235) for 1g 20s. Sold by Alliance: Leonard Porter (Western Plaguelands), limited stock; Horde: Werg Thickblade (Western Plaguelands), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 15725 nearest

step Pattern: Runic Leather Headband
  tip Pattern: Runic Leather Headband teaches Runic Leather Headband (Leatherworking 265) for 2g 20s. Sold by Jase Farlane (Eastern Plaguelands), limited stock. Its sellers keep one or two in stock that come back some time after a sale; it binds when picked up, so the Auction House never has it.
  buy 15756 nearest

step Get Runecloth
  tip 500 Runecloth for Leatherworking 225-300: 50 Runic Leather Headbands. Humanoids of level 45-60 drop it, and what you loot as you level counts. The arrow takes you to the best farm for your level: mobs at or below it first, then the most Runecloth per minute and the nearest; it picks again as you level. The guide window shows the kills and minutes it takes there and a second choice. Or buy them at the Auction House.
  collect 14047 x500 nearest gather levels 45-60
  auction 14047 x500

step Skin Rugged Leather
  tip 145 Rugged Leather for Leatherworking 225-239: 29 Rugged Armor Kits; from your skinning on the way: 75 of 145 Rugged Leather. Skin 70 Rugged Leather at the areas of Skinning 275-300, the richest in it (they give no more points), then craft 23 Rugged Armor Kits (Leatherworking 225 to 239). The window lists the Skinning areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests there until your bags hold them.
